# autostereogram

- Label: Auto Stereogram
- Category: Copernicus (`Cop`), Houdini 22.0.368
- Inputs: 0 to 2
- Parameters: 6 (exact, read from Houdini by hython)
- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/autostereogram.html
- Summary (EN): Creates a flat image that shows a 3D illusion when the viewer looks past its surface. It samples a repeating texture and warps the sampling coordinates according to a depth image.
- Résumé (FR) : Produit une image stéréogramme qui cache une illusion de relief, en déformant l'échantillonnage d'une texture selon une carte de profondeur.

- Inputs meaning: ["source: pattern sampled to form the stereogram", "depth: depth image; larger values make that area appear more raised"]

- Key parameters: ["Scale: sampling frequency of the source; higher values repeat the texture more often", "Depth Range: clamps depth values so results stay stable", "Border: sampling beyond the input edges; defaults to the layer border property", "Re-Center: when on, distortion spreads outward from the center; when off, it applies left to right"]

- Caveats: ["Depth values must be positive", "A Remap COP placed before the node can bring depth values into a usable range", "Use Mirror for textures that do not tile naturally, and Wrap for textures that do", "A Scale that is too high can produce noise that cannot be resolved"]

